From b06779e9c7a5e92fdd858e1d56634dcecb92d3bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:44:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A game object flagged to glow carries a soft light at its
 highest point (GAMEOBJECT_FLAGS 0x08000000)

`GO_FLAG_GLOW`, Basin Battle's own bit beside the preview and stretch bits: the object draws a soft
white additive sprite about half a yard across, facing the camera, pulsing gently (0.55 to 0.85
over 1.6 s), at the top of its world bounds, and a small white point light sits at the same spot,
a carried torch's strength over a few yards. The top is taken from the model's box under the
object's own transform, so a planted arrow glows at its fletching above the grass whichever way
the model's axes run. Both come with the object and go with it; an object without the bit draws
nothing new. For the Hunter's arrows planted in the ground, which were lost in the grass at night.
